      "bio_summary": {
        "value": "Harriet Maxine Hageman (born October 18, 1962) is an American politician and attorney serving as the U.S. representative for Wyoming's at-large congressional district since 2023. She is the Republican nominee for the 2026 United States Senate election in Wyoming , seeking to succeed incumbent Cynthia Lummis . [ 1 ] A Wyoming native, Hageman holds degrees from the University of Wyoming and has spent her career as a trial attorney. She unsuccessfully ran for the Republican nomination for governor of Wyoming in 2018 and later served as a member of the Republican National Committee . ",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harriet_Hageman",
        "source_type": "wikipedia"
